App.tsx with ListState imported from types.

Careful: `useDebouncedValue` returns q; effect dependencies include q.

Also need to avoid initial fetch before `me` loaded. Use `me` gate.

Potential issue: when actor changes, `me` stays old until new fetch resolves; I should clear me immediately. In the actor effect, `setMe(null)`.

Implement `refresh` counter.

`meError` — if fetch fails, list stays loading; show banner. Set list to error? When me is null and meError set, list remains loading; better set list error message. Simpler: when meError, show banner and table not rendered? Table requires state; pass `{kind:"error", message}`? Let me handle: if meError, render a full-card error banner instead of table? Keep table with error state:

```tsx
const effectiveList: ListState = meError ? { kind: "error", message: meError } : list;
```
and retry → reload me (bump). onRetry should refetch me too: define `retryAll` = () => { setMeError(null); setRefresh(v=>v+1); setActorTick? }. The me effect depends on actorEmail only; add `meReload` state to dep.

Let me add `const [meReload, setMeReload] = useState(0)` and effect deps [actorEmail, meReload]. Retry handler: `setMeError(null); setMeReload(v=>v+1); setRefresh(v=>v+1);`.

Export button disabled when !me.

Header: show tenant chip only when me.

For details, pass timezone: `me?.tenant.timezone ?? "UTC"`.

Toast.

Let me write App.tsx.

Also note React 19: no need for React import with jsx runtime.

App:

```tsx
import { useEffect, useState } from "react";
import { ApiError, downloadCertificateExport, fetchCertificates, fetchMe, messageOf } from "./api";
import { useDebouncedValue } from "./hooks";
import type { ListResponse, ListState, Me, SortDir, SortField } from "./types";
import { Toolbar } from "./components/Toolbar";
...
```

List fetch:
```tsx
useEffect(() => {
  if (!me) return;
  const controller = new AbortController();
  setList({ kind: "loading" });
  fetchCertificates(actorEmail, { q, sort, dir, page, pageSize }, controller.signal)
    .then((data) => setList({ kind: "ready", data }))
    .catch((error: unknown) => {
      if (error instanceof DOMException && error.name === "AbortError") return;
      setList({ kind: "error", message: messageOf(error) });
    });
  return () => controller.abort();
}, [me, actorEmail, q, sort, dir, page, pageSize, refresh]);
```
`me` object identity changes on reload; fine.

Stale page after filtering: effect setPage(1) triggers refetch; there may be a transient request with old page → abort ordering handles via cleanup (abort previous). Actually both effects run; first render fetch with page=3 then setPage(1) → new fetch; old aborted. Fine.

When q changes to a value with fewer pages, page resets to 1 ✓.

Display `list.data.total` in toolbar: `list.kind === "ready" ? list.data.total : null`.

Details onChanged: `(message) => { setRefresh(v => v+1); setToast({kind:"success", text: message}); }`.

Bulk onCompleted same.

Export:
```tsx
async function handleExport() {
  setExporting(true);
  try { await downloadCertificateExport(actorEmail, { q, sort, dir }); setToast({kind:"success", text:"CSV export downloaded"}); }
  catch (error) { setToast({kind:"error", text: messageOf(error)}); }
  finally { setExporting(false); }
}
```

Sorting:
```tsx
function handleSort(field: SortField) {
  if (field === sort) setDir(d => (d === "asc" ? "desc" : "asc"));
  else { setSort(field); setDir(field === "issued_date" ? "desc" : "asc"); }
}
```

Header content.

Empty state for no courses? Bulk dialog handles.

